    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_07a03668856c26d8a5bfd65b584eb2e973b121979c63bacb6fb01087d16fb4b0",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The two directions of the Hardy-space closure equivalence use sharply asymmetric mechanisms. Under RH, finite Mobius-weighted generator combinations converge through a regularized intermediate object and a zero-geometry-derived norm majorant to the target E. If RH fails, one zero rho in Omega makes every F_lambda vanish, so continuous evaluation at rho places their entire closed span in a proper kernel while E(rho) remains nonzero.",
