    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_698e7b9967c54eecb4611576ff14b429d031ece9fa40354fb56ed50f37a08075",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The source links one RH closure problem across four Hilbert representations by explicit maps: the Mellin isometry sends each fractional-part generator f_lambda to -F_lambda and the constant target 1 to E; reciprocal specialization places g_l=f_{1/l} in the step-function space M; and unitary reciprocal-integer sampling sends 1 and each g_l to gamma and gamma_l. Target closure is therefore preserved for the corresponding families, while totality is separately established in L2 and M and transferred unitarily from M to the sequence space.",
