    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_9176a7ecb149235e090ac5a369beea0f0b6dd78ddf7507386c75f244438617e2",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The continuous and discrete closure-to-totality proofs instantiate the same cyclic-orbit mechanism. In each case a closed generator span is invariant under a multiplicative semigroup of isometries; once it contains the distinguished target, it contains that target's orbit, which corresponds to a known-total family of interval indicators and therefore forces the generator span to be the whole relevant source space.",
