    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_a5e6a39d1f169d53a40056a1a0c66fc92c833aa50a820367d393dbec858ef438",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The constructive implication realizes approximate inversion of zeta in two controlled limits. Mobius-weighted finite combinations of the discrete Hardy generators first converge at fixed horizontal shift to a regularized reciprocal-zeta object; RH-dependent zero geometry then supplies domination for removing the shift in Hardy norm. Because the Mobius coefficients vanish off square-free integers, the same construction uses only the square-free-indexed generators.",
