    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_e11f27d31795f45c510835c75416403806519d86129292d1b5d2f094f65b0b1a",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The unitary sequence representation turns the infinite density criterion into a nested family of finite projection problems: RH is equivalent to the distance D(L) from gamma to the first finite generator span tending to zero. Standard Hilbert-space projection then expresses each squared distance as a ratio of Gram determinants, yielding a finite-dimensional observable while exposing an estimability bottleneck rather than a proof route already under control.",
